      "transferReality": "The real bottleneck isn't any single timetable — it's the Ginzan Cart's 6-seat, no-reservation, first-come-first-served design. A party of 8 should expect to split across 2 cart departures or have part of the group walk; nothing about that is stated on the operator's own booking flow because there IS no booking flow.",
      "groupLuggageMobility": "The Matsue→Odashi leg carries all trip luggage (this is the intake's stated 'main regional transfer between bases'), which slows platform transfers and rules out a rushed connection. For the 2 low-mobility travelers, the 2.3km/45min walking fallback at the mine is a real exertion cost, not a footnote — factor it into who takes the first cart.",
      "buffer": "Arrive Odashi by early-to-mid afternoon to leave enough cart cycles (≈30-40 min apart) for a group split, plus slack before the last practical train.",
      "missedConnection": "Missing the last practical Odashi→Matsue train (≈19:24) means either a taxi covering a very long rural distance or an unplanned night in Oda City without a booked room.",
      "nextService": "Not confirmed this pass whether a later, slower local service exists after 19:24 — treat 19:24 as the hard deadline until reconfirmed.",
      "lastPracticalReturn": "≈19:24 ex-Odashi (Super Oki service toward Yonago, calling at Matsue)",
      "fallback": "A taxi from Odashi to Matsue (long and expensive, not priced this pass) or an unplanned hotel night in Oda City center."
    }
